  <prompt>Amend `projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md` SC #2 to allow the "retired-on-disk-with-banner" convention adopted by Wave G-6 (for AzCli*, PacAdmin*, PowerShellAppConfigSeeder, DeployBffApiScriptRunner, and now PlaceholderInvariantVerifier retirements). Current SC #2 requires grep-verify to return zero matches for retired shell-out class names — but Wave G-6 accepted retention of files with a retirement banner header (preserves audit trail + prevents accidental resurrection). Task 202's verification matrix B21 row flagged this as DESIGN CONFLICT ("SC #2 says grep should return zero; Wave G-6 accepts on-disk-with-banner"). Amend SC #2 to explicitly allow retired-on-disk-with-banner as a valid completion state, update the verification recipe, and cross-reference `PlaceholderInvariantVerifier.cs` retirement banner as the current example.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform architect. Familiar with: project spec.md § Success Criteria structure; SC #2 current wording + verification recipe; Wave G-6 retired-on-disk-with-banner convention (adopted 2026-08-XX for AzCli*/PacAdmin*/PowerShellAppConfigSeeder classes and now for PlaceholderInvariantVerifier when 204c retires it); the retirement-banner header format (used in `PlaceholderInvariantVerifier.cs` per punch list B07 row citation).</role>

  <goal>`projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md` SC #2 amended to:
- Allow retired-on-disk classes that carry a retirement-banner header as a valid completion state (in addition to fully-deleted classes)
- Updated verification recipe: `grep -L "// RETIRED" <candidate-files>` (find files that DO NOT have the banner) instead of `grep -c <class-name>` (find any occurrence)
- Cross-reference `PlaceholderInvariantVerifier.cs` retirement banner as current example
- Retain prohibition on ACTIVE registration of retired classes (banner is on-disk-only; DI module must NOT `services.AddSingleton<TInterface, RetiredClass>()`)

Punch list B21 row annotated `applied 2026-XX-XX task 204g — spec.md SC #2 amended`.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Wave G-6 (~2026-08-XX) adopted a pattern: when a class is superseded (AzCliKvSecretsWriter → real KV writer; DeployBffApiScriptRunner → artifact-fetch handler; PowerShellAppConfigSeeder → C# seeders; PlaceholderInvariantVerifier → real probes), the class file remains ON DISK with a retirement-banner header explaining:
- WHEN retired
- WHICH task retired it
- WHAT replaced it
- WHY retained on disk (audit trail; prevents future author from re-creating class with same name unknowingly)

The DI module registrations are removed, so the class is UNREACHABLE at runtime — but the file preserves history.

Current spec.md SC #2 verification recipe is (paraphrasing task 202 B21 row): `grep -c "<retired class name>" src/` should return zero. But Wave G-6 convention retains the file → grep still returns non-zero → SC #2 literal check FAILS despite class being effectively retired.

Task 202 verification matrix B21 flagged this as **DOWNGRADE — spec-amendment task**. Amendment reconciles SC #2's intent (no active retired classes) with Wave G-6's implementation (on-disk-with-banner audit trail).

**Why post-186 safe**: spec amendment only; no code / runtime impact. Also unblocks any future task 204c retiring PlaceholderInvariantVerifier via same convention (currently SC #2 would fail that retirement literally).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="input">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/task-202-punch-list.md B21 row + verification matrix</file>
      <file role="modify">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md § Success Criteria § SC #2 (amend wording + verification recipe)</file>
      <file role="reference-example">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/E2EAcceptance/PlaceholderInvariantVerifier.cs (retirement banner header — current example for spec cross-reference)</file>
      <file role="reference-earlier-examples">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/**/AzCli*.cs + PacAdmin*.cs + PowerShellAppConfigSeeder.cs + DeployBffApiScriptRunner.cs (earlier retirement-banner examples)</file>
      <file role="update">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/task-202-punch-list.md B21 row annotation</file>
    </relevant-files>
