  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (MINIMAL, sonnet/high). Read `notes/task-202-punch-list.md` B21 row.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Read + verify current SC #2 wording">Read `projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md` § Success Criteria § SC #2 verbatim. Confirm wording matches punch list description (grep-verify recipe requires zero occurrences).</step>
    <step order="2" name="Read retirement-banner reference examples">Read the retirement-banner header of `PlaceholderInvariantVerifier.cs` (current example) + at least one earlier Wave G-6 example (`AzCliKvSecretsWriter.cs` OR `DeployBffApiScriptRunner.cs`) to capture the banner format for spec cross-reference.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Amend SC #2">Update spec.md § SC #2:
- Preserve intent statement (retired shell-out / placeholder classes MUST NOT be actively used)
- Add: "Retired classes MAY be retained on-disk with a retirement-banner header (Wave G-6 convention) — this preserves audit trail + prevents accidental resurrection under the same class name. Retention-with-banner is a valid completion state."
- Replace verification recipe with: `grep -L "// RETIRED" <candidate-files>` (files matching the retired-class name pattern but LACKING the banner header) OR (equivalent): `grep <retired-class-name> src/server/services/**/*Module.cs` (any DI module actively registering the retired class → FAIL). Combined check ensures class is not actively registered AND if retained on-disk has banner.
- Cross-reference: "Example: `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/E2EAcceptance/PlaceholderInvariantVerifier.cs` retirement banner header format (retired by task 204c per punch list B07)."</step>
    <step order="4" name="Annotate + report">Update `notes/task-202-punch-list.md` B21 row: `applied 2026-XX-XX task 204g — spec.md SC #2 amended per Wave G-6 retired-on-disk convention`. Update `current-task.md`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If spec.md SC #2 wording has been amended since punch list verification pass (2026-08-24 SESSION 7), STOP + escalate — punch list state may be stale + amendment premise may not apply.</trigger>
    <trigger>If retirement-banner header format is inconsistent across earlier Wave G-6 retirements, standardize as part of amendment (author canonical banner template inline in SC #2) + open follow-on row for updating older retirements to conformant format.</trigger>
  </escalation>

