  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Amendment-only (edit existing spec); §11 does not trigger. Cost-of-doing-nothing: SC #2 literal check keeps failing on every Wave G-6-convention retirement (AzCli* / PacAdmin* / PowerShellAppConfigSeeder / DeployBffApiScriptRunner / soon PlaceholderInvariantVerifier via task 204c), forcing either false-negative acceptance or spec violation ambiguity. Amendment reconciles SC #2 intent with adopted convention.

**Post-186 safe + also unblocks 204c**: amendment must land BEFORE task 204c retires PlaceholderInvariantVerifier (204c's Step 11 relies on Wave G-6 convention being spec-sanctioned). If 204c runs first + retires the placeholder + SC #2 amendment lags, SC #2 literal check fails on 204c's own output.</notes>

